			"advancement": "lepidodendron:pf_adv_book_walterosteus",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Walterosteus is a genus of selenosteid known from Frasnian aged rock in the town of Bad Wildungen in Germany and the Kellwasser Facies of the Anti-Atlas Mountains in Morocco. 3 species are known, those being W. pachyosteides, W. lelievrei, and W. grossi. The first two are known from skulls around 5-6 centimeters in length, while the more fragmentary W. grossi is thought to have grown larger."
		},
		{
			"advancement": "lepidodendron:pf_adv_book_walterosteus",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Walterosteus was once considered synonymous with Enseosteus, however this view is now considered inaccurate."
